      "pronunciationText": "Back to our point, pi over six, a half. The tangent's gradient is minus root three. Flip it and change the sign, and the normal's gradient is one over root three, which is root three over three. Quick check: minus root three, times one over root three, is minus one. Same point, new gradient. So the normal is y minus a half equals root three over three, times x minus pi over six. The only new work was the gradient. The point didn't change. On the road, the headlights follow the tangent, and the line straight across the road follows the normal."
    },
